      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-07-12_WidnesExaminer_art0187" n="art0187">
        <head>By Mr. FRANK HICKMAN.</head>
        <p>By Mr. FRANK HICKMAN.</p>
        <p>SALE OF HOUSEHOLD FURNITURE AND EFFECTS AT 38, ARPLEY-STREET, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>lAR. FRANK ' HICKMAN WILL SELL BY AUCTION ON TUESDAY, JULY 15. 1913, by instructions of Mrs. Daniel lUD, who is going to Canada, the HOUSEHOLD FURNITURE AND EFFECTS, Comprising Brass Fire Suite, Fire Screen' Marble Clock and Bronzes, Ebonised Over mantel, Solid Walnut Work Table, Ebonised Palm Stand and Plant, Drawing Room Suite (7 pieces) in Figured Velvet and So lid Walnut Frames, Mahogany Oval Table, Walnut Cabinet with Mirror Doors and i3ack,Walr.ut Occasional Table,Capital Pianoforte in Ebony Case, by W. G. Eavestaff ; Music Stool, Oak Hall Stand, Dining-roorn Suite in Tapestry, Mahogany Dining Table, Walnut Bookcase and Chiffonier, Easy Chairs, Mahogany frame, Walnut Overmantel, Oil Painting and Pic.,ures, Inlaid Linoleum, Pole and Blinds, 8-day Grandfather Clock in Oak Case (by Joyce, of Whitchurch), 6ft. Massive Oak Side- board with Cellarette and Bevelled Plate Back, Capital Square Tube Brass Bedstead, Wire and Fleck biattreszes Black and Brass Bedsteads, Hair Mattresses, Feather Beds, 3ft. Gin. Walnut Bedroom Suite, Birch Chest of Drawers, Birch Washstand and Dressing Table, Commode, Toilet Ware, Vases, Ceno Chairs, Massive Stair Rods and Eyes, Axminster Stair Carpet, Wood Chairs, Mahogany Frame Sofa, Extending Dining Table, Nlallogany Chairs upholstered in Leather, Gas Grill, Rocker, Brass Preserving Pan, Saucepans, Kitchen Dresser, Wringer, Dolly and Tuts, Pair steps and Sundry Articles. Sale to commence at 2 o'clock prompt. Auctioneer's Offices, Lyme-street, Warricgtor. Telephone 331 y.</p>
        <p>UNRESERVED SALE AT 31, GR APPENHALL- ROAD, STOCKTON HEATH, WARRINGTON (by instructions of the Executors of the late Mrs. William Dutton.) MR FRANK HICKMAN WILL SELL BY 'AUCTION AS ABOVE ON THURSDAY AND FRIDAY NEXT, JULY 17T11 AND 18TH, 1913. The whole of the superior HOUSEHOLD FURNISHING EFFECTS. Linen, Books, Silver, Electro-Plate, Crayon Draw- ings by George Sheffield, Mahogany Secretaire, Turkey and Al irzapore Carpets, Badroom furnishings by Garnetts, Bath Chair and outside effects. The lota comprise: Garden Roller, Garden Seat with Awning, Hose and Reel, Garden Tools, Washirg TubF, Wringer,Kito hen and Scullery Utensils, Dresser, Tables, Chairs, Dinnerware, Teaware, Tinware, Saucepans,Bath- chair, nearly new, with hood ; 8-day Clock, Mirror, set plated Dish Covers, Brass Pans,kitchen Cutlery,enclosed Dresser Glass, Glass Dishes, Wedgwood Teapot, Tea and Coffee Service, old oak Cupboard inlaid with mahogany, 3 Brass Preserving Pans, brass Kettle, brass Mortar, Copper Kettle, ' brass Tray copper Ornaments, brass Coffee Maker, Brownware contents of Cellars, contents of two Attics, Brass and Black Bedsteads, Wood's Wire Yattresses, Hair Mattresses, Feather Beds, Bolsters, Pillows, Oak Linen Chest, Tapestry Curtains, Lace Curtairs, Sheets, Blankets, Quilts, Eiderdown Quilts, Bed Linen, Table Linen Covers and Tray Clothe, Towels, 3-ft. Combina- tion Bedsteads and Wood's Wire Mattresses, -I-ft. Satin Walnut Bedroom Suite, cane Chairs,Cornice Poles and Curtains, Brass Bedsteads, Painted Wardrobe and Bed- room Suite, Art Squares, Toiletware, Trinket Sets, antique mahogany Tables Night Chair, Lady's Dress- ing Case, copper Coal Scuttle, Medicine Chest, quantity of Wines, Old Tawny Port and Champagne ; Mahogany, Bedroom Suite, all fitted and complete, made by Garnett and Sons, Warrington ; Pedestal Cupboard, Axminster Stair and Landing Carpet and Brass Stair Rods, Brass Trap, Plants and Fardiniere?, air Horns, Engravings, Mats' Card Table inlaid with satinwood, Barometer in oak case, by Knott and Co. ; coloured Crayon Drawing in Eoglish gilt frame, by George Sheffield ; Curbs, Fire Steels, Brass Fire Guard, 3 large Engravings, 300 volumes of Books, mahogany Butler's Tray and Stand, Beadwork Trays and Fire Screens,brass Bell, marble Clock, marble Horses and Figures, capital Oak Frame Suite in Morocco Leather, Oak Frame Couch, Walnut Sidehoard and Dinnemagon, cut Decanters, cut Finger Bowls, Claret Jug, Champagne, Hock, Port and Sherry Wineglasses, Custard and Jelly Glasses, cut and engraved Goblets, seven.' cases of Fish and Fruit Eaters, Case of Cutlery, silver Sugar Tongs, silver Tea Spoons, Georgian silver Cream Jug, solid silver sleigh and Stag, costly design, silver- plated Tray and Tea Urn with Spirit Lamp (very heavy), 6-hole Cruet, set Carvers, Knives, Prong., Spoons,Salad Bowl and Servers, Oak Tray,Gravy Spoons, Te3,Dessert and Table Spoons ; Brass Letter Rack, Turkey Carpet, Oak Coal Box and Scoop, Dining-room Suite in oak frames, 6 Feather Cushions, Pollard Oak Sideboard with plate glass tack, lined with mahogany, made by Garnett's ; psir of handscmely chased brass Ewers, Mirzapare Carpet?, mahogany carved Ckairs, Oil Paintings in et frames, flive fine Crayon prawines by G.sorg,e Sheffield, 10 iVater Colour 4Drawings, Lot of Old China •Sporlo Sugar Basin and Cups, Cloisonne Vase Dese:t Service, lot "s.!•_e!i, Bon Bon Dishes, Dresden Ornaments, Worcester Vase, 4 Walnut Framed Chairs in Silk Tapestry, 3 Lady's Occasional Chairs, Lady's Davenport Walnut Inlaid, pair handsome Vases, hrrd-raintei ; Burr Walnut French Cabinet with brass headings, Music CaLinet, mahogany inlaid Grandfather Clock, S-day with brass and silvered dial in fine condition ; CbiNaendale !thogany 13weou ar.d Display Ccb'net, Walnut lOyainant.l bud (Aber EffeA.4. Catalogues from the Aucticnc, Sale to commence each day at 11 o'ciccii prompt. View Day : Weekesdar, day prior to Sale, 1 to 4 p.m. Admission by Catalogue. Office, Lynit-street, Warring