        <p>ANGLING NOTES. Warrington Workingmen's Angling Association (N.A. Centre). _— Sport during the holidays was very indifferent. Some were disappointed, but others put specimens on the board, gudgeon, chub, perch, and roach, all finding a place at Headquarters. The Bay Horse shield match takes place at Hartford to-morrow (Sunday), start 7.30 a.m. from Bay Horse, the match to commence at 11 20. NOTICE. Warrington Anglers must make it their duty to close all gates after they have passed through, especially at Mickle Trafford, as complaints have been made to the secretary at headquarters. An execative council meeting will be held at the Gladstone Arms on Thursday next at 8 p.m. Secre- taries please notify their delegates. A LIST OF SPECIAL PRIZES. We append a list of special prizes offered for com- petition in connection with the Northern Anglers' Association, Members must be in benefit before they can compete : SET BOARD PRIZES.—Bream : 1, Gs. ; 2,2 s. Chub : 1, Gs.; 2,2 s. Trout : 1, 63. ; 2,2 s. Perch : 1, Gs. ; 2, 2s. Roach : 1, Gs. : 2,2 s. Daco : 1, Gs. ; 2,2 s. Gudgeon : 1, Gs. ; 2, 2.. SPECIAL PRlZES.—lloach from Norton : 1, 103.; 2,</p>
