        <p>STOCKTON HEATH, LATCEIFORD AND WARRINGTON. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION BY MESSRS JOHN MAINWARING AND CO., at the Blue Bell Hotel, Horsemarket-street, Warrington, on WEDNESDAY, the 23rd JULY, 1913, at 5 p.m , subject to Conditions of Sale then to be produced and react. Lot I.—A VALUABLE PLOP of FREEHOLD BUILDING LAND containing 2,COS square yards or thereabouts situate on the southerly side of Whitetield- road, Stockton Heath, and having a frontage thereto of 100 feet or thereabouts. This land is most pleasantly situated and is excellently suited for the erection of detached or semi-detached villas. Lot 2.—SEVEN .MESSUAGES or DWELLING. HOUSES (" Littleniore's-row ") being 2,3, 4,5, 6, 7 and 8, Kimberley-drive, Stockton Heath, in the respec- tive occupations of Mr. William Houghton and ethers. Gross rentals £55 14s. Tenure—freehold, subject to a net yearly rent charge of £2B 4s. sd. Lot 3.—A SEMI-DETACHED DWELLING-HOUSE called "Thorn Lea," Grappenhall-road,Stockton Heath, in the occupation of Mr. C. D. Parkinson. Gross annual rental £34. Tenure—leasehold for .999 years from 2nd August, 1896, subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of £3 73. scl. Lot 4.—A SEMI-DETACHED DWELLING-HOUSE called "Helvetie," G rapp, nhall-road, Stock ton Heathein the occupation of Mrs. Hewitt. Gross annual rental £3O. Tenure—leasehold for 929 years from 2nd August, 1896, subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of £3 7s. 4d. NOTE.—Lots 3 and 4 will first be offered together in ore lot at the net total yearly payable ground rent of £6 14s. 93. Lot 5.—A DETACHED DWELLING-HOUSE called " Ashlea House," Grappenhall-road, Stockton Heath, in the occupation of Mrs. Henry Milling. Gross annual rental £5O. Tenure—leasehold for 1,000 years from lith May. 19G, subject to a net payable yearly ground rent of kb 2s. 10d. Lot 6.—A SEMI-DETACHED DWELLING-HOUSE, No. 24, Whitefleld-road, Stockton Heath, with large garden thereto, in the occupation of Mr. John Newcombe as yearly tenant. Gross yearly rental £26. Tenure—sub-leasehold for 919 years (except thn last 21 days thereof) from Ist May, 1901, subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of £4 2s. Gd. Lot 7.—A SEMI-DETACHED DWELLING-HOUSE, No. 26, Whitefield-road, Stockton Heath, with garden thereto, in the occupation of the Rev. William Reid as yearly tenant. Gross yearly rental £25. Tenure— sub-leasehold for 999 sears (except the last 21 days) from Ist May, 1901, subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of £3 7s. Gd. NOTE.— Lots 6 and 7 will first be offered together in one Lot, subject to a total yearly ground rent of £7 10e. Lot B.—A DWELLING-HOUSE, 117, London-road, Stockton Heath, in the occupation of Mr. M. B. Robinson. Gross rental £l9 15s. per annum. Tenure— leasehold for 999 years from 2nd August, 1901, subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of £1 15s. 4d. Lot 9.—A DWELLING-HOUSE, 119, London-road, Stockton Heath, in the occupation of Mr. Alfred Jolley. Gross rental £l9 103. per annum. Tenure— leasehold for 999 years from 2nd August, 1901, subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of £l. 15s. Si. Lot 10.—A DWELLING-HOUSE, 121, Lotdon-road, Stockton Heath, in the occupation of Mr. George Johnson. Gross rental £lO 103. per annum. Tenure— leasehold for 999 years from 2nd August, 1901, subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of £1 15s. 53. NOI:E. Lots 3,9, and 10 will first be offered together in one Lot subject to a total net payable y early ground rent of £5 6s. 2d. Lot 11.—THE DESIRABLE FREEHOLD FAMILY RESIDENCE, called "Latchford Lodge," Lower Wash- lane, Latchford, in the occupation of Mr. Robert Lowe as yearly tenant. The house contains entrance hall, dining, drawing and breakfast rooms, 4 bedrooms, and boxrocni, bathroom and w.c. ; larder and outside offices, together with two-stall stable and coach-house and garden. Lot 12.—A FREEHOLD MESSUAGE OR DWELLING-HOUSE called "Willow Cottage, " Wilderspool Causeway, Warrineton, in the occupation of Mr. Isaac Newton as tenant thereof, with the garden, yard and appurtenances thereto, containing altogether 49:3 superficial square yards or thereabouts. Gross rental £2O per annum. F.r further particulars apply :—As to Lots 1,2, 3,4, and, 3 to Mr. Thomas Ridgway, Solicitor, Warrington ; as to Lot 5 to Messrs.. Henry Greenall and Co., Solicitors, Warrington; as to Lot 11 to Mr. J. Longland, Solicitor, Warrington ; and RS to all the Lots to the Auctioneers, Bridge-straet, Warrington ; or to MESSRS. ROBERT DAVIES &amp; CO. Solicitors, Wart ngton.</p>
